  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The dominant finding is that switching the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200 (config_026 vs config_019, all else identical) produced a massive accuracy jump from 0.542 to 0.706, making scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted the clear best configuration. The most important untested dimension for this winning combination is the aggregation strategy: avgpool vs. transformer. With scgpt, avgpool was marginally better (0.542 vs 0.520), but the scvi_n200 latent representation may interact differently with transformer attention, potentially capturing cross-profile dependencies that simple pooling misses. config_027 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a single-variable change from the current best, directly testing whether transformer aggregation can push accuracy beyond 0.706. This is the highest-value experiment because it either confirms avgpool as optimal (reducing uncertainty and focusing remaining budget on other axes) or discovers a new best configuration, and it is the most natural logical extension of the strongest evidence in the search."
}

